---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import type { SeoMetadata } from '@/lib/seo';

const seo: SeoMetadata = {
  title: 'About NatalNode',
  description: 'NatalNode is building a clearer, more transparent way to calculate, inspect, and understand a natal chart.',
  canonical: '/about'
};
---

<SiteLayout seo={seo} mode="editorial">
  <main class="nn-container nn-container--editorial pb-20 pt-12 sm:pb-24 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="nn-eyebrow">ABOUT NATALNODE</p>
      <h1 class="nn-type-page-title mt-3">A clearer way to read a chart.</h1>
      <p class="nn-type-body mt-4 max-w-2xl">
        NatalNode is building a clearer, more transparent way to calculate, inspect, and understand a natal chart—combining professional chart UX, structured chart facts, clear interpretation, and calculation transparency.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl space-y-12 sm:mt-16 sm:space-y-16">
      <section class="border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-8 sm:pt-10" aria-labelledby="why-title">
        <p class="nn-eyebrow">Why NatalNode exists</p>
        <h2 class="nn-type-section-title mt-2" id="why-title">Keep the layers visible.</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 nn-type-body">
          <p>
            A chart can become one opaque result: calculation, interpretation, and presentation blended together. NatalNode keeps those layers distinct so you can tell what was calculated, what is interpretive, and what is unavailable or limited.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-8 sm:pt-10" aria-labelledby="calculation-title">
        <p class="nn-eyebrow">Calculation before interpretation</p>
        <h2 class="nn-type-section-title mt-2" id="calculation-title">Start with explicit chart facts.</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 nn-type-body">
          <p>
            The product direction is straightforward: Birth input → chart calculation → structured chart facts → interpretation. NatalNode.com is the first-party Web product around the NatalNode Engine boundary, presenting interpretation grounded in the facts returned there.
          </p>
          <p>
            Any future AI explanation would sit after those facts; it would not calculate them or fill in what is missing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-8 sm:pt-10" aria-labelledby="uncertainty-title">
        <p class="nn-eyebrow">Uncertainty stays visible</p>
        <h2 class="nn-type-section-title mt-2" id="uncertainty-title">Unknown should stay unknown.</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 nn-type-body">
          <p>
            An unknown birth time can leave time-dependent parts of a chart unavailable. Historical timezone ambiguity may need to be surfaced for a user to choose between possible occurrences, and provenance may not be available for every result.
          </p>
          <p>
            NatalNode should show those limits instead of creating false precision. The product does not treat an unavailable fact as an invitation to guess.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-8 sm:pt-10" aria-labelledby="inspectability-title">
        <p class="nn-eyebrow">Inspectability</p>
        <h2 class="nn-type-section-title mt-2" id="inspectability-title">A chart should not be a black box.</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 nn-type-body">
          <p>
            When available, Calculation Details can expose calculation status, Engine version, chart schema, configuration status, provenance, and warnings alongside the result.
          </p>
          <p>
            Not every field is present in every result. Showing what is known—and what is not—is part of making the chart easier to inspect.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-8 sm:pt-10" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
        <p class="nn-eyebrow">Product direction</p>
        <h2 class="nn-type-section-title mt-2" id="direction-title">Build toward clearer understanding.</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 nn-type-body">
          <p>
            Planned work is focused on better chart understanding, richer deterministic interpretation, additional professional chart tools, and stronger Learn and reference tools. Future capabilities will stay on the same Engine-first boundary and will be labeled future or planned until they are ready.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a
              class="inline-flex font-semibold text-natal-accent underline decoration-natal-accent/50 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-white"
              href="/methodology"
            >
              Read our methodology →
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
